{{also|sjå|sją̊}}
==Icelandic==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|non|is}} {{m|non|séa}}, {{m|non|sjá}}, from {{etyl|gem-pro|is}} {{m|gem-pro|*sehwaną}}, from {{etyl|ine-pro|is}} {{m|ine-pro|*sekʷ-||to see, notice}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈsjauː/|lang=is}}
*: {{rhymes|auː|lang=is}}

===Verb===
{{is-verb-strong|sá|sáu|séð}}

# to [[see]], to [[sense]] or [[perceive]] with one's [[eye]]s
#: '''''Sérðu''' illa?'' — ''Nei, ég '''sé''' mjög vel.''
#:: Have you got bad eyesight? — No, I '''see''' very well.
# to [[see]], to [[perceive]], to [[spot]]{{jump|is|spot|s}}
# to [[see]], to [[understand]]{{jump|is|understand|s}}
#: {{ux|is|Þú hlýtur að '''sjá''' hvað þetta er asnaleg hugmynd!|You must '''see''' what a stupid idea this is!}}

